### WhatsApp Business Calling — enable SIP via Graph API
### Use with VS Code REST Client or import into Postman.
### SIP can ONLY be enabled here, NOT in the Meta UI.
###
### Fill these:
@VERSION = v21.0
@PHONE_NUMBER_ID = REPLACE_WITH_PHONE_NUMBER_ID
@TOKEN = REPLACE_WITH_SYSTEM_USER_ACCESS_TOKEN
@HOST = sip.codentra.pk
@PORT = 5061

### 1) Enable SIP + register our server (SDES for first bring-up)
POST https://graph.facebook.com/{{VERSION}}/{{PHONE_NUMBER_ID}}/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "calling": {
    "status": "ENABLED",
    "sip": {
      "status": "ENABLED",
      "webhook_delivery": "ENABLED",
      "servers": [
        {
          "hostname": "{{HOST}}",
          "port": {{PORT}},
          "request_uri_user_params": { "tenant": "1" }
        }
      ]
    },
    "srtp_key_exchange_protocol": "SDES"
  }
}

### 2) Retrieve the Meta-generated SIP password + app_id
### (requires whatsapp_business_management, Advanced access)
GET https://graph.facebook.com/{{VERSION}}/{{PHONE_NUMBER_ID}}/settings?include_sip_credentials=true
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN}}

### -> calling.sip.servers[0].sip_user_password  => Asterisk .env META_SIP_PASSWORD
### -> calling.sip.servers[0].app_id             => Meta dialog "App ID" field

### 3) (If needed) Rotate the password: disable, empty servers, then re-run step 1.
POST https://graph.facebook.com/{{VERSION}}/{{PHONE_NUMBER_ID}}/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "calling": { "status": "ENABLED", "sip": { "status": "DISABLED", "servers": [] } }
}

### 4) Subscribe the app to the `calls` webhook field (so call_created/terminate fire)
POST https://graph.facebook.com/{{VERSION}}/{{WABA_ID}}/subscribed_apps
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN}}
### (set @WABA_ID above; subscription field config is done in App Dashboard > Webhooks > whatsapp_business_account > calls)
